{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TT-303 ACID MACHINE \u8212- mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303. Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL TUNING semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents CUTOFF filter frequency, ~150 Hz .. ~2 kHz exponential (rises with resonance) RESONANCE feedback of the 18 dB ladder up to self-oscillation ENV MOD depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves DECAY decay of the filter envelope, ~30 ms .. ~570 ms ACCENT level AND filter boost of the accent circuit WAVEFORM sawtooth / square\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish documentation)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Filter: 3-pole ladder (18 dB/oct) in ZDF/TPT form, level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled, then 3-point decimation. Soft clip only at the master, never in the OS loop (it never engages there at real levels anyway).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes): mild peak correction; the resonance hump moves up with rising resonance, as on the reference.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Feedback HP 20 Hz IN the feedback path (DC block).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Square with frequency-dependent duty + tilt, classic 1-sample PolyBLEP.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accent capacitor: recharge +0.95, saturation 1.65. Accent sweep with non-linearity and slight cutoff dependency.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab On accent: fixed 0.2 s filter decay + shortened VCA attack (1.8 ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Slide: constant time, log frequency space; the same note stays held.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPERATING MODES HOST Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll. Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide. SEQ Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length. Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN). MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out. All four banks travel with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Effect path: ahead of each of the three units \u8212- WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/ Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb \u8212- sits an input EQ as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry signal runs alongside untouched. On the drive what the EQ removes is added back after the WaveShaper, so a raised lowcut takes the bass out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output (drive off = transparent).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI: THRU at the top of the header passes INCOMING notes on to the output (CC and pitchbend always pass through anyway). SEQ OUT in the sequencer panel sends the SELF-GENERATED sequence out. Two different sources, hence two switches. In SEQ mode incoming notes are transpose commands \u8212- whoever also passes them on with THRU sends them out next to the sequence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White, Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads. Wordmark in Zilap Orian, if installed. Labels sans-serif (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New). Which of these is present the script measures itself. The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the window size \u8212- to enlarge, just drag the FX window open. HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is exclusively via the device front.\par}
}

